::ENG4_U01_L08_GP_Q1::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Independent learning does not mean working without support. Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which paraphrase preserves the claim? {
=A. Independent learners take responsibility while using support thoughtfully.#Correct. This preserves the qualified idea.
~B. Independent learners never use support.#This contradicts the passage.
~C. Independent learning means avoiding feedback.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. Independent learners do not revise work.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_GP_Q2::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. What does deliberately mean? {
~A. Accidentally#This is the opposite.
~B. Without thinking#This is the opposite.
~C. Silently#This is unrelated.
=D. Intentionally and purposefully#Correct. Deliberately means on purpose.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_GP_Q3::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: Effective independent learners use resources deliberately, ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work. Which sentence follows standard conventions? {
~A. Effective learners asks focused questions.#The subject and verb do not agree.
=B. Effective learners ask focused questions, evaluate feedback, and revise their work.#Correct. The series is clear and conventional.
~C. Effective learners ask focused questions evaluate feedback and revise work.#Commas are needed for clarity.
~D. effective learners ask focused questions.#The sentence begins with a lowercase letter.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_GP_Q4::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: A student who studies the feedback can identify the pattern behind the mistake. Which oral explanation is most coherent? {
~A. Feedback is there and mistakes happen.#This is vague.
~B. Mistakes are bad, so feedback is feedback.#This is circular.
=C. Studying feedback supports independent learning because it helps students recognize patterns in mistakes.#Correct. This gives claim, evidence, and rationale.
~D. Students should not examine feedback.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L08_GP_Q5::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Strong independent learning therefore depends on both personal responsibility and thoughtful use of available support. Which phrase must be preserved in a paraphrase? {
~A. Only personal responsibility#This omits support.
=B. Both personal responsibility and thoughtful use of support#Correct. The passage emphasizes both.
~C. Only available support#This omits responsibility.
~D. Neither responsibility nor support#This contradicts the passage.
}
